              not detected in the patient. Thus, it remains unclear whether the
              molecular alteration in SGBS cells is also responsible for the
              high differentiation capacity and further investigations are
              required. CONCLUSION: The human cell strain described here
              provides an almost unlimited source of human preadipocytes with
              high capacity for adipose differentiation and may, therefore,
              represent a unique tool for studying human fat cell development
              and metabolism. International Journal of Obesity (2001) 25, 8-15",
  journal  = "Int. J. Obes. Relat. Metab. Disord.",
