                 measures designs",
  author      = "Hoffman, Gabriel E and Roussos, Panos",
  abstract    = "SUMMARY: Large-scale transcriptome studies with multiple
                 samples per individual are widely used to study disease
                 biology. Yet, current methods for differential expression are
                 inadequate for cross-individual testing for these repeated
                 measures designs. Most problematic, we observe across multiple
                 datasets that current methods can give reproducible
                 false-positive findings that are driven by genetic regulation
                 of gene expression, yet are unrelated to the trait of
                 interest. Here, we introduce a statistical software package,
