               understanding of how differentiation is maintained in healthy
               tissues or altered in a disease state, and 2) - our ability to
               use cell fate reprogramming for regenerative purposes. Here,
               using a genome-wide transcription factor screen followed by
               validation steps in a variety of reprogramming assays (cardiac,
               neural and iPSC in fibroblasts and endothelial cells), we
               identified a set of four transcription factors (ATF7IP, JUNB,
               SP7, and ZNF207 [AJSZ]) that robustly opposes cell fate
               reprogramming in both lineage and cell type independent manners.
